        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0279" n="271" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.115 Eastern States Petroleum Co./66:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-06T13:00:00+00:00">February 6, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 6—10:54 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>443. My telegram No. 441, February 2, 1 p.m.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d245-f1"/>
                    There can be no doubt that Sangroniz acted at once on my first letter for in
                    acknowledging my second just received he says: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I have received your letter of the 29th instant relative to the capture
                            of the Steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Nantucket Chief</hi>.</p>
                        <p>As it is always pleasing for me to attend to the matters which you submit
                            to my consideration, I hasten to inform you that previous to your letter
                            and note with reference to the above mentioned steamer the necessary
                            orders had been given in order that the <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Nantucket Chief</hi>, its captain and crew should be placed at
                            liberty.</p>
                        <p>I know that you will appreciate and communicate to your Government the
                            deep feeling of generosity which is contained in the gesture of His
                            Excellency the Chief of State the incarnation of National Spain.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
